'==============================================================================
' Real-world scenario: the controller of a public DC fast-charge post for
' electric vehicles. The state machine describes one object - one charge post -
' over its whole lifetime, from mains being applied to decommissioning.
'
' Every notation from the Sparx Systems UML 2 "State Machine Diagram" tutorial
' appears at least once; the legend at the foot of the diagram says where.
'
' Render with:  java -jar plantuml.jar -tsvg charge-post-state-machine.puml
'==============================================================================
@startuml charge-post

title Public DC Fast-Charge Post — Controller State Machine

!includesub charge-post-state-machine.puml!COMMON

<style>
state {
  ' A terminate pseudo-state is drawn as a bare cross, so the state box around
  ' the glyph is styled away and the glyph itself is used as the label.
  .terminate {
    LineColor transparent
    BackgroundColor transparent
    FontSize 34
    FontColor #B00020
    shadowing 0
  }
  .submachine {
    BackgroundColor #EEF3FF
  }
}
</style>

'============================================================ top-level lifetime
' Terminate pseudo-state and a named final state.
state "✕" as HardStop <<terminate>>
state "Decommissioned" as Decommissioned <<end>>

' A state with entry, exit, do and on-event actions.
state PoweringUp
PoweringUp : entry / runSelfTest()
PoweringUp : do / blinkAmber(1 Hz)
PoweringUp : mainsSag / holdSelfTest()
PoweringUp : exit / logSelfTest(result)

' Initial pseudo-state, and a transition with trigger [guard] / effect.
[*] --> PoweringUp : mains applied
' Self-transition: a failed self test is retried without leaving the state,
' which is worth drawing because the transition carries an effect.
PoweringUp -[nonode]-> PoweringUp : selfTestFailed [attempt < 3]\n/ attempt++ ; rearmRelays()
PoweringUp --> OutOfService : selfTestFailed [attempt >= 3]\n/ postFault(F01)
PoweringUp --> InService : selfTestPassed / announceAvailable()

'============================================================== in-service scope
state InService {

  [*] --> [H]

  ' Shallow history: returning from ServiceMode resumes the sub-state that was
  ' interrupted, but anything nested inside that sub-state starts afresh.
  ' The outgoing transition is the default taken when there is no history yet.
  [H] --> WaitingForDriver

  state WaitingForDriver
  WaitingForDriver : entry / showWelcome()
  WaitingForDriver : do / pollRfidReader()
  WaitingForDriver : screenIdle(30 s) / dimDisplay()
  WaitingForDriver : exit / clearDisplay()

  ' Another self-transition: an unreadable card is re-read in place.
  WaitingForDriver -[nonode]-> WaitingForDriver : cardPresented [!isReadable] / beep(2)

  '--- Compound state, second notation: the ⊕ marks a sub-machine whose details
  '--- are drawn in a separate diagram. Only its entry and exit points show.
  state "Authorising" as Authorising <<submachine>> {
    state "full" as authFull <<entryPoint>>
    state "cachedToken" as authCached <<entryPoint>>
    state "authorised" as authOk <<exitPoint>>
    state "refused" as authNo <<exitPoint>>
    ' hidden edges only, to keep the four pins from crowding each other
    authFull -[hidden]right-> authCached
    authOk -[hidden]right-> authNo
  }

  ' Into the sub-machine's normal way in ...
  authFull <-- WaitingForDriver : connectorInserted [connectorLocks()]\n/ lockConnector()
  ' ... and into a named entry point that skips reader initialisation.
  authCached <-- WaitingForDriver : cardPresented [tokenCached && isReadable]\n/ reuseToken()

  '--- Choice pseudo-state: a dynamic branch, evaluated on values that were
  '--- only measured during the state that has just been left.
  state PickProfile <<choice>>
  authOk --> PickProfile
  PickProfile --> ChargeSession : [request.kW > 150 && pack.degC < 35]\n/ setLimit(500 A)
  PickProfile --> ChargeSession : [request.kW > 150 && pack.degC >= 35]\n/ setLimit(125 A) ; warnDerated()
  PickProfile --> ChargeSession : [else]\n/ setLimit(request.kW)

  '--- Junction pseudo-state: two routes chained into one static branch.
  state RetryOrBlock <<junction>>
  authNo --> RetryOrBlock
  SessionAbandoned --> RetryOrBlock
  RetryOrBlock --> WaitingForDriver : [strikes < 2] /\lunlockConnector();\lshowRetry()
  RetryOrBlock --> CardBlocked : [strikes >= 2] / captureAudit()

  state SessionAbandoned
  state CardBlocked
  CardBlocked : entry / holdCard(60 s)
  CardBlocked --> WaitingForDriver : holdExpired / unlockConnector()

  '--- Compound state, first notation: the sub-machine is drawn in place.
  '--- Power delivery and cable cooling run concurrently while energy is
  '--- being delivered, each as its own composite state entered from a fork
  '--- and synchronised on a join before the session ends - the same
  '--- fork/join idiom as Finalising Session below, needed here because
  '--- PlantUML cannot render a fork whose targets sit in separate
  '--- `--`-separated regions.

  state "Charge Session" as ChargeSession {

    state DeliveringEnergyFork <<fork>>
    state ChargeSessionJoin <<join>>

    [*] --> [H*]
    [H*] --> DeliveringEnergyFork

    '=== power delivery ===
    state "Power Delivery" as PowerDelivery {
      [*] --> RampingUp

      state RampingUp
      RampingUp : entry / closeContactors()
      RampingUp : do / rampCurrent(20 A/s)
      RampingUp --> ConstantCurrent : currentStable [insulationOk]

      '--- Nested compound state: constant-current delivery is itself a small
      '--- machine, because the current that can be held is traded against pack
      '--- temperature. This nesting is what gives the deep history above
      '--- something to do: a shallow history would resume Constant Current at
      '--- FullRate, whereas [H*] resumes it in the derated sub-state the
      '--- session was actually in when the grid browned out.
      state "Constant Current" as ConstantCurrent {
        [*] --> FullRate

        state FullRate
        FullRate : do / holdCurrent(limit)
        FullRate --> Derated : pack.degC > 45 / warnDerated()

        state Derated
        Derated : do / holdCurrent(limit * 0.6)
        Derated : exit / clearDerateBanner()
        FullRate <-- Derated : pack.degC < 38
        Derated --> Throttled : pack.degC > 52 / postFault(F31)

        state Throttled
        Throttled : entry / requestPackCooling()
        Throttled : do / holdCurrent(30 A)
        Derated <-- Throttled : pack.degC < 48
      }

      ' Transition off the frame of the nested compound state: it fires from any
      ' of the three sub-states, and their exit actions run on the way out.
      ConstantCurrent --> ConstantVoltage : soc >= 80 % / logKnee()
      ConstantVoltage : do / holdVoltage(pack.vMax)
      ConstantVoltage --> ToppingOff : current < 8 A
      ToppingOff --> [*] : soc >= target || driverStop
    }

    '=== cable and stack cooling ===
    state "Cable Cooling" as CableCooling {
      [*] --> CoolantIdle

      state CoolantIdle

      '--- Second nested compound state, so both composites carry a nested
      '--- configuration for the deep history to restore.
      state "Coolant Running" as CoolantRunning {
        [*] --> PumpModerate

        state PumpModerate
        PumpModerate : entry / pump(50 %)
        PumpModerate : do / logCableTemp(1 Hz)
        PumpModerate --> PumpBoost : cable.degC > 65\n/ pump(100 %) ; fansMax()

        state PumpBoost
        PumpBoost : do / logCableTemp(4 Hz)
        PumpModerate <-- PumpBoost : cable.degC < 60 / pump(50 %) ; fansAuto()
      }

      CoolantIdle --> CoolantRunning : cable.degC > 45
      CoolantIdle <-- CoolantRunning : cable.degC < 40 / pump(0 %)
      CoolantIdle --> [*] : deliveryComplete
      CoolantRunning --> [*] : deliveryComplete / purgeLoop()
    }

    DeliveringEnergyFork --> PowerDelivery
    DeliveringEnergyFork --> CableCooling

    ' No trigger: each fires on completion of its own composite, and the
    ' join does not fire until both have completed.
    PowerDelivery --> ChargeSessionJoin
    CableCooling --> ChargeSessionJoin
    ChargeSessionJoin --> [*]
  }

  state Suspended
  Suspended : entry / openContactors() ; showHoldMessage()
  Suspended : do / monitorGrid()
  Suspended <-- ChargeSession : gridBrownout / openContactors()

  ' Deep history: after the brownout the session resumes the exact nested
  ' configuration it was interrupted in - both regions, at the sub-state each
  ' one had reached, and inside Constant Current or Coolant Running at the
  ' derate or pump level it had reached too - rather than restarting the
  ' session. A shallow [H] here would restore Constant Current but drop back
  ' to FullRate, which is the difference the nesting makes visible.
  Suspended --> ChargeSession : gridRestored [insulationOk]\n/ closeContactors()
  Suspended --> SessionAbandoned : holdTimeout(15 min) / endSessionEarly()

  '--- Fork and join: once delivery is complete, releasing the connector and
  '--- settling the payment run as two concurrent threads that are then
  '--- synchronised before the post offers itself to the next driver.
  state "Finalising Session" as Finalising {
    state ReleaseFork <<fork>>
    state ReleaseJoin <<join>>
    [*] --> ReleaseFork
    ReleaseFork --> UnlockingConnector
    UnlockingConnector : entry / unlockConnector()
    UnlockingConnector --> ReleaseJoin : cableStowed
    ReleaseFork --> SettlingPayment
    SettlingPayment : entry / captureFunds(kWh * tariff)
    SettlingPayment --> UploadingRecord : captureOk
    UploadingRecord --> ReleaseJoin : cdrAcknowledged
    ReleaseJoin --> [*]
  }

  ' No trigger: this fires on completion of the Charge Session state.
  ChargeSession --> Finalising
  Finalising --> WaitingForDriver : / printReceipt()
}

'=========================================================== service and faults
state ServiceMode
ServiceMode : entry / inhibitPower()
ServiceMode : do / streamDiagnostics()
InService --> ServiceMode : serviceDoorOpened\n/ logAccess(technician)
InService <-- ServiceMode : serviceDoorClosed / rearmRelays()
OutOfService <-- ServiceMode : technicianLocksOut / postFault(F99)

state OutOfService
OutOfService : entry / showOutOfService()
OutOfService : do / reportFaultToCpo(every 5 min)
OutOfService --> ServiceMode : technicianAuthenticated
OutOfService --> Decommissioned : decommissionCommand / wipeCredentials()

' Terminate pseudo-state: the controller's lifeline ends here. No exit actions
' run and nothing happens again until the post is physically power-cycled.
InService --> HardStop : emergencyStopPressed\n/ openContactors() ; ventCoolant()
ServiceMode --> HardStop : emergencyStopPressed / openContactors()

note right of HardStop
  Terminate pseudo-state: the
  lifeline of the state machine
  ends; no exit actions run.
end note

note bottom of Decommissioned
  Named final state.
end note

legend bottom
  |= Tutorial element |= Where it appears in this diagram |
  | State | PoweringUp, WaitingForDriver, Suspended, ... |
  | Initial and final states | [*] --> PoweringUp ; Decommissioned |
  | Transition (trigger [guard] / effect) | selfTestFailed [attempt < 3] / attempt++ |
  | State actions (entry / exit / do / on event) | PoweringUp, WaitingForDriver, Suspended |
  | Self-transition | PoweringUp, WaitingForDriver |
  | Compound state, drawn in place | Charge Session, Finalising Session |
  | Compound state, nested three deep | Constant Current, Coolant Running (in Power Delivery / Cable Cooling, in Charge Session) |
  | Compound state, separate diagram | Authorising ⊕ |
  | Entry point | full, cachedToken (on Authorising ⊕) |
  | Exit point | authorised, refused (on Authorising ⊕) |
  | Choice pseudo-state (dynamic branch) | PickProfile |
  | Junction pseudo-state (static branch) | RetryOrBlock |
  | Terminate pseudo-state | the cross reached on emergency stop |
  | History state, shallow | InService [H] — return from ServiceMode |
  | History state, deep | Charge Session [H*] — resume after a brownout,\ndown into Constant Current / Coolant Running |
  | Fork and join | DeliveringEnergyFork, ChargeSessionJoin in Charge Session; ReleaseFork, ReleaseJoin in Finalising Session |
endlegend

@enduml

'==============================================================================
' The AuthoriseDriver sub-machine referenced by the Authorising ⊕ state above.
'==============================================================================
@startuml authorise-driver

title AuthoriseDriver — sub-machine of the Authorising state

!includesub charge-post-state-machine.puml!COMMON

state "AuthoriseDriver" as AuthoriseDriver {

  ' Entry and exit points sit on the frame of the sub-machine, and match the
  ' pins shown on the Authorising ⊕ state in the parent diagram.
  state "full" as epFull <<entryPoint>>
  state "cachedToken" as epCached <<entryPoint>>
  state "authorised" as xpOk <<exitPoint>>
  state "refused" as xpNo <<exitPoint>>

  ' The normal way in: initialise the reader first.
  [*] --> InitialisingReader
  epFull --> InitialisingReader

  state InitialisingReader
  InitialisingReader : entry / powerReader()
  InitialisingReader : do / handshakeReader()
  InitialisingReader : exit / clearReaderBuffer()
  InitialisingReader --> AwaitingCredential : readerReady
  InitialisingReader --> xpNo : readerFault(3 tries) / postFault(F12)

  ' Named entry point: when a token is already cached the initialisation is
  ' unnecessary, so the sub-machine is entered at ValidatingToken instead.
  epCached --> ValidatingToken

  state AwaitingCredential
  AwaitingCredential : do / awaitTapOrApp()
  AwaitingCredential -[nonode]-> AwaitingCredential : credentialSeen [!wellFormed] / beep(2)
  AwaitingCredential --> ValidatingToken : credentialCaptured / hash(credential)
  AwaitingCredential --> xpNo : idleTimeout(60 s) / showTimeout()

  state ValidatingToken
  ValidatingToken : entry / queryBackOffice()
  ValidatingToken : do / spinner()
  ValidatingToken --> xpOk : tokenAccepted / issueSessionId()
  ValidatingToken --> OfflineWhitelist : backOfficeUnreachable(5 s)

  state OfflineWhitelist
  OfflineWhitelist --> xpOk : [tokenOnWhitelist] / flagDeferredBilling()
  OfflineWhitelist --> xpNo : [else] / showTryLater()
}

note right of AuthoriseDriver
  Two named exit points, so the state
  the parent machine enters next depends
  on the route taken out of here:
  authorised → the choice pseudo-state,
  refused → the junction pseudo-state.
end note

@enduml

@startuml common-elements

!startsub COMMON

!pragma edgeCornerRadius 5

hide empty description

skinparam stateDiagramEdgeLabelStyle node
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rankSep 20

!endsub

@enduml
